# core/data/talk/grammar/en/beats_lines.tlk - the drama manager's own lines (owner: TK;
# T6 starter bank: about 5 a beat so every beat is heard; the content package
# after T6 writes the ~500). Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py. docs/TALK.md
# "The drama manager".
#
# beat.<name>   a beat's goal line: what the residents try to get in while
#               the room is in that beat (core/data/talk/beats.tlk); each rule
#               is guarded beat=<name>. Said to the player.
# idle          one resident to another when the player says nothing for 8 s
# prod          then, after two of those, someone prods the player
# excuse        the one whose engagement ran out, on the way to the door
# grumble       the one another resident cut off
# jab, row, ultimatum   the three steps of an argument (rivalry); with a child
#               in the room only the jab is ever said (talk_dm.c), and the
#               two later steps are guarded !kid_present here as well
# makeup        after the player made peace
# kidask        a child in the room of an argument: the room cools down
#
# Kid-safe everywhere but beat.romance_adult (adults the gate passed, with
# the one addressed saying yes: consent). No register word in this file.

# ---- ARRIVE ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.arrive guard: beat=arrive act: tell
  "Shoes off. Or on. The rug bites either way."
  "You made it! We were about to talk about you."
  "Sit, sit. That chair is haunted, but politely."
  "Perfect timing. Nothing was happening. On purpose."
  "Welcome in, {you}. Touch nothing that hums."

# ---- SMALLTALK ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.smalltalk guard: beat=smalltalk act: tell
  "Weather's odd today. The fog waved at me."
  "Long day. Short day? One of those days."
  "It's quiet out. I don't trust it."
  "I counted the clouds earlier. There were some."
@rule beat.smalltalk.ask guard: beat=smalltalk act: ask_about
  "So, {you}. What's new? Lie if you have to."
  "Anything on your mind? Take your time. Not too much."

# ---- TOPIC_DIVE: the fan talks it up ----------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.topic_dive guard: beat=topic_dive&topic act: opine_pos
  "Wait. We're on {x}? Clear my evening."
  "Oh, I have THOUGHTS about {x}. Sit down."
  "{x:cap}! Finally, a real subject."
  "I could talk about {x} for an hour. I will."
  "Nobody leaves until we've done {x} justice."

# ---- HOUSE ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.house guard: beat=house act: tell
  "I like this room. It has opinions."
  "That lamp is doing its best. Bless it."
  "Cosy in here. Suspiciously cosy."
  "Did the wall always look at us like that?"
  "Nice place, {you}. The floor only creaks in jest."

# ---- GOSSIP ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.gossip guard: beat=gossip act: gossip
  "Did you hear the news? I heard it twice. It grew."
  "I'm not one to gossip. Anyway, listen to this."
  "You didn't hear it from me. I heard it from me."
  "Big news in town. Nobody agrees what it was."
  "Somebody's in the paper again. I'm not saying who."

# ---- PROBLEM: the troubled one opens up -------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.problem guard: beat=problem&fact.problem act: complain
  "Can I say something? I've had a rough week."
  "I'm fine. That was a lie. Hello."
  "Something's been on my mind. It pays no rent."
@rule beat.problem.lonely guard: beat=problem&prob=lonely act: complain
  "It's been quiet at mine. Too quiet. I miss noise."
@rule beat.problem.bored guard: beat=problem&prob=bored act: complain
  "I am so bored I alphabetised my socks."
@rule beat.problem.nightmare guard: beat=problem&prob=nightmare act: complain
  "I had the dream again. The one with the stairs."

# ---- ALLY_ASK: "Back me up here." ---------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.ally_ask guard: beat=ally_ask act: ask_opinion
  "Back me up here, {you}."
  "{you}, tell them I'm right. Take your time."
  "You agree with me, {you}. I can see it in your face."
  "Tie-breaker! {you}, it's on you. No pressure."
  "{you}. Settle this. Wrong answers will be noted."

# ---- STORY: in-world worry, no spoilers -----------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.story guard: beat=story act: tell
  "The purple fog's early this year. It never knocks."
  "Strange days. Even the crows look worried."
  "Things feel off lately. Like a picture hung crooked."
  "I keep my bag packed. Snacks, mostly."
  "Something's coming. I hope it's cake."

# ---- GAME: a lull -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.game guard: beat=game act: ask_about
  "Game time. Would you rather fight a goose or be one?"
  "Quick. Guess my favourite food. You get one go."
  "Would you rather have no knees or too many?"
  "Let's play. I spy something beginning with dust."
  "Truth or truth, {you}. We're out of dares."

# ---- KID_MOMENT: the kid says it -----------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.kid_moment guard: beat=kid_moment&kid_speaker tags: kid act: tell
  "I can burp the alphabet. Up to D."
  "Grown-ups talk a lot. When do you get to the point?"
  "I found a bug. His name is Kevin. He lives here now."
  "Is this the boring part? It feels like the boring part."
  "When I'm big I'm going to be a dragon. Or a dentist."

# ---- ROMANCE_ADULT: adults the gate passed; it always ends on a joke (R2) -------------------
@rule beat.romance_adult guard: beat=romance_adult&consent&adults_only&!kid_present&!pet act: flirt
  "Stay for dinner, {you}. My soup is nearly legal."
  "Keep smiling at me like that and I'll burn the toast."
  "[LOVE]You make this dump feel like a date, {you}."
  "I cleaned for you. Under the rug counts as clean."
  "You, me, one candle. It's a power cut, but still."

# ---- WIND_DOWN --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.wind_down guard: beat=wind_down act: farewell
  "Well, this was nice. Nobody cried much."
  "It's getting late. The clock is judging us."
  "Good talk. I'll be thinking about it by accident."
@rule beat.wind_down.promise guard: beat=wind_down act: promise
  "Come by again, {you}. I'll hide the good biscuits."
  "Same time next week? I'll bring the chairs."

# ---- idle chatter: one resident to another --------------------------------------------------
@rule idle.ask guard: to_res&topic act: ask_about
  "So, {them}. Still into {x}?"
  "{them}, settle a bet. {x:cap}: yes or no?"
  "Hey {them}. Remind me why you like {x}."
@rule idle.plain guard: to_res act: ask_about
  "{them}, what did you do today? Keep it short."
  "So, {them}. Read any good signs lately?"
@rule idle.tease guard: to_res&rel=rival act: tease
  "{them}, you're quiet. It suits you."
  "Still wearing that face, {them}? Brave."
@rule idle.muse guard: !to_res act: tell
  "Quiet in here. I can hear the fridge thinking."
  "Nobody talk at once. Oh. Nobody is."
  "I'll just hum, then. Mm. That was the hum."

# ---- the prod -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule prod act: ask_feeling
  "You're very quiet, {you}."
  "{you}? Blink twice if you're still in there."
  "Say something, {you}. Anything. A vowel."
  "Hello, {you}? It's your turn. It has been for a while."

# ---- walking out ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule excuse act: farewell
  "I left something on the hob."
  "Is that the time? It is. Bye."
  "I just remembered a thing. Elsewhere."
  "My plants need me. They said so."
  "I'm going to go stare at a wall. A different one."

# ---- cut off by another resident --------------------------------------------------------------
@rule grumble act: complain
  "I was TALKING."
  "Excuse me. I had a whole sentence planned."
  "Fine. I'll finish it in my head. It was good."
  "Rude. I was nearly at the point."

# ---- an argument: the jab (the only step with a child in the room) ------------------------
@rule jab guard: to_res act: tease
  "Nice hat, {them}. Did it lose a bet?"
  "{them} would know. {them} knows everything."
  "Oh, {them} has an opinion. Mark the calendar."
  "Funny. Coming from you, {them}."
  "Sure, {them}. And I'm the mayor's left shoe."

# ---- step 2: the row --------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule row guard: to_res&!kid_present act: accuse
  "That's it, {them}. You've been like this all week!"
  "You always do this, {them}. I keep a list."
  "Don't you start, {them}. I will finish."
  "Say that again, {them}. I'm taking notes."
  "You borrowed my ladder in spring, {them}. SPRING."

# ---- step 3: the ultimatum (the player is told to take a side) -------------------------------
@rule ultimatum guard: to_res&!kid_present act: ask_opinion
  "{you}, pick. Me or {them}. Right now."
  "One of us is leaving, {you}. You choose who."
  "{you}, it's {them} or me. No pressure. Lots, in fact."
  "Enough. {you}, tell {them} I'm right."

# ---- making up (a mediation that worked) ------------------------------------------------------
@rule makeup guard: to_res act: apologize
  "Fine. Sorry, {them}. You're only mostly wrong."
  "All right, {them}. Truce. I was a bit much."
  "Sorry, {them}. Keep the ladder. It likes you."
  "Peace, {them}. For {you}. And for my blood pressure."

# ---- a child in the room of an argument -------------------------------------------------------
@rule kidask guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: ask_feeling
  "Are you guys fighting?"
  "Why are you using your angry voices?"
  "Is this a fight? Should I get snacks?"
  "You two sound like the crows again."
